  "notes": "USAGE:\n{立案|りつあん} refers to the initial stage of creating a plan or proposal. It is more formal than {計画|けいかく}を{立|た}てる and is often used in organizational or governmental contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {政策|せいさく}を{立案|りつあん}する (to draft a policy)\n- {立案者|りつあんしゃ} (planner, author of a plan)\n- {立案|りつあん}{段階|だんかい} (planning stage)\n- {企画|きかく}{立案|りつあん} (project planning)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{企画|きかく} focuses on conceiving creative projects or events, while {立案|りつあん} focuses on the formal drafting of plans and strategies. {策定|さくてい} is an even more formal term for establishing official policies.",
